 "deviations": [
  {
   "item": "11.2(a) t_utc / order_index columns",
   "handling": "The harness writes no per-session timestamp and no shuffle position. Per-BATCH start/end UTC are recorded in results/expB/batch_plan.json and added as columns to the merged CSVs, so the 5.2 arm-centre figure and V4/V5 time regressions are computable at batch resolution, not session resolution."
  },
  {
   "item": "11.2(c) --anchor injection every 40 sessions",
   "handling": "The harness cannot inject anchor cells inside a batch. Both anchors are measured in their own invocations at every batch BOUNDARY instead (16 boundaries x 2 anchors x --anchor-reps sessions), on the single 1.30.0 interpreter, into results/expB/b_drift_anchor.csv. V4's first-third / last-third medians are computable; the time resolution is one boundary (20-70 min) instead of ~3 min."
  },
  {
   "item": "11.2(e) --not-applicable removal before the shuffle",
   "handling": "--exclude takes family:variant pairs and cannot express a per-RELEASE exclusion, so the NOT-APPLICABLE (file, release) cells of 3.0 cannot be removed from a batch without splitting the batch by release group - which would confound release with invocation and destroy the within-batch shuffle that 5.2 requires. They are therefore left in the grid, where they fail at session construction in ~1 s and are recorded as status=FAILED rows carrying the runtime's own error text. No timing is produced for them; the analysis drops them by name from every denominator using results/expB/load_probe.json. --exclude IS used for any (family, variant) that stage 0 shows fails on EVERY release, which is release-independent and so expressible."
  },
  {
   "item": "11.1 artefact paths",
   "handling": "The protocol puts the CSVs under results/paper/. This run round is allowed to write only scripts/paper/b_run.py, results/expB/* and D:/sec_work/*, so every artefact keeps its registered FILE NAME under results/expB/ instead. Nothing under results/paper/ is written."
  },
  {
   "item": "7 release-notes retrieval",
   "handling": "Stage 0's notes retrieval is implemented (--stage notes) but is OFF by default: it is the one step that needs the network, and downloading is not done unprompted."
  }
 ],
